WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:03.167
-Thank you for coming
back to the show.

00:00:03.167 --> 00:00:04.734
-Yeah.

00:00:04.734 --> 00:00:06.501
-You have
so many accomplishments.

00:00:06.501 --> 00:00:08.200
I want to run through them

00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:10.434
so right now we understand
what's happening here.

00:00:10.434 --> 00:00:13.000
First of all, since the last
time you were on our show,

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:15.634
BTS has been nominated
for five Grammys.

00:00:15.634 --> 00:00:19.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:19.734 --> 00:00:22.901
Your single "Seven" made history

00:00:22.901 --> 00:00:24.701
by being the fastest song
in history

00:00:24.701 --> 00:00:27.334
to reach 1 billion streams.
1 billion.

00:00:27.334 --> 00:00:32.467
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:32.467 --> 00:00:37.434
A few weeks ago, you replaced
yourself on Spotify's list

00:00:37.434 --> 00:00:39.968
of most streamed songs
in the world.

00:00:39.968 --> 00:00:46.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:46.601 --> 00:00:51.334
And now your debut solo album
"Golden" is out

00:00:51.334 --> 00:00:53.267
and it's already
breaking all sorts of records.

00:00:53.267 --> 00:00:56.934
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:56.934 --> 00:00:59.734
Oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh!

00:00:59.734 --> 00:01:01.534
I have news for you.

00:01:01.534 --> 00:01:03.868
I have news for you that I don't
even know if you know this yet.

00:01:03.868 --> 00:01:05.200
This just happened an hour ago.

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:08.100
Your single "Seven" just became
platinum right now.

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:10.868
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:10.868 --> 00:01:12.567
Come on now!

00:01:12.567 --> 00:01:20.100
♪♪

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:22.267
Congratulations.
-Thank you.

00:01:24.567 --> 00:01:25.834
-How does it all feel?

00:01:25.834 --> 00:01:30.000
Are these things
that you imagined were possible?

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:32.868
-You...

00:01:32.868 --> 00:01:37.334
You really make it sound
like I'm a huge global pop star.

00:01:37.334 --> 00:01:39.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:39.300 --> 00:01:40.868
-Well, yeah. This helps.

00:01:40.868 --> 00:01:43.100
Yes, yes, I think you are.
I think you are, yeah.

00:01:56.767 --> 00:01:59.267
[ Crowd cheers ]

00:02:05.634 --> 00:02:07.267
Yeah.
[ Crowd cheers ]

00:02:09.901 --> 00:02:12.234
The best fans.

00:02:12.234 --> 00:02:15.534
Before we get into the album,
I want to learn more about you.

00:02:15.534 --> 00:02:18.901
When you're not breaking records
and being a global pop star,

00:02:18.901 --> 00:02:22.601
what do you like doing?

00:02:22.601 --> 00:02:25.334
Outside of music,
what do you do for fun?

00:02:25.334 --> 00:02:29.300
-I think...

00:02:29.300 --> 00:02:33.200
uh, it's -- hmm.

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:36.501
Pretty ordinary,
like many people.

00:02:36.501 --> 00:02:41.868
Like, sometimes I spend
my whole day in bed.

00:02:41.868 --> 00:02:43.868
[ Laughter ]

00:02:43.868 --> 00:02:47.200
Or cooking.
-Ooh, cooking?

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:48.968
-Working out.
-Yeah.

00:02:48.968 --> 00:02:51.767
[ Crowd cheers ]

00:02:51.767 --> 00:02:54.801
What do you cook?
What do you like to cook?

00:02:54.801 --> 00:02:56.501
-Do you know...

00:02:56.767 --> 00:02:58.667
[ Crowd cheers ]

00:03:00.167 --> 00:03:01.734
-No.
-Noodle.

00:03:01.734 --> 00:03:05.367
-Yes!
[ Laughter ]

00:03:05.367 --> 00:03:07.100
I love noodles, yes.

00:03:07.100 --> 00:03:10.033
Yes, I know that. You slurp?

00:03:10.033 --> 00:03:12.200
Yeah, yeah, yeah.
That's the way to do it.

00:03:15.501 --> 00:03:17.067
[ Crowd cheers ]

00:03:17.067 --> 00:03:18.934
Alright.
Yes, I will do that.

00:03:18.934 --> 00:03:21.400
But also I heard that you like
making your own pizza.

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:23.234
-Pizza. Ah. Yeah.

00:03:23.234 --> 00:03:28.367
-Yeah?
-I like pizza, but...

00:03:28.367 --> 00:03:33.267
I didn't like leftovers, so...

00:03:33.267 --> 00:03:35.434
-So like cold pizza, no good?
-Yeah.

00:03:35.434 --> 00:03:38.167
-Well, have you ever had
New York City pizza?

00:03:38.167 --> 00:03:39.634
-Not yet.

00:03:39.634 --> 00:03:41.934
[ Crowd cheers ]

00:03:41.934 --> 00:03:43.467
Oh!
-I got you...

00:03:43.467 --> 00:03:46.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:46.033 --> 00:03:48.567
I got you. It's not cold.

00:03:48.567 --> 00:03:50.767
-New York pizza!

00:03:50.767 --> 00:03:52.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:52.968 --> 00:03:55.801
-This is one of my favorite --

00:03:55.801 --> 00:03:57.200
This is one of my favorite --
-Your favorite?

00:03:57.200 --> 00:03:59.434
-Yeah. This is what I like.
This is Joe's Pizza.

00:03:59.434 --> 00:04:00.734
-Let's cheers.
-Cheers, bud.

00:04:00.734 --> 00:04:02.567
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:02.567 --> 00:04:14.767
♪♪

00:04:14.767 --> 00:04:15.868
That's good, right?

00:04:15.868 --> 00:04:18.801
-Yum!
-Yeah. I'm talking about!

00:04:18.801 --> 00:04:22.801
I have more questions for you.
I have more questions for you.

00:04:22.801 --> 00:04:25.968
I was looking through
some interviews with you,

00:04:25.968 --> 00:04:27.400
and this question made me laugh.

00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:30.834
It said, what is
the scariest thing in the world?

00:04:30.834 --> 00:04:32.000
The scariest thing
in the world for you,

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:34.133
and your answer was...

00:04:34.133 --> 00:04:36.734
Does anyone know?
-Microwave!

00:04:36.734 --> 00:04:40.234
-Yes, a microwave.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:40.234 --> 00:04:42.367
A microwave.

00:04:42.367 --> 00:04:44.501
"I always worry
that it will explode."

00:04:44.501 --> 00:04:47.133
What are you talking about?

00:04:47.133 --> 00:04:49.000
-Well, when I was young...

00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:54.067
-Yeah.
-I used to be afraid, but...

00:04:58.100 --> 00:04:59.467
Still afraid.

00:04:59.467 --> 00:05:01.167
[ Laughter ]

00:05:01.167 --> 00:05:04.067
-Why? Why are you afraid?

00:05:04.067 --> 00:05:06.734
-I don't know.

00:05:06.734 --> 00:05:08.400
-I guess it's a little
frightening,

00:05:08.400 --> 00:05:11.100
because I don't
really understand it.

00:05:11.100 --> 00:05:13.300
-I don't know, like...
-Yeah.

00:05:13.300 --> 00:05:14.868
-Boom.
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:05:14.868 --> 00:05:16.300
No, nothing is going to happen.

00:05:16.300 --> 00:05:19.033
No, nothing's going to happen.
Nothing is going to happen.

00:05:19.033 --> 00:05:21.667
You'll be fine with
the microwave, but I understand.

00:05:21.667 --> 00:05:23.767
I don't understand
how it does get warmer,

00:05:23.767 --> 00:05:26.701
but maybe I'll research that
and I'll learn.

00:05:26.701 --> 00:05:32.501
I was looking that you go
on this livestream sometimes

00:05:32.501 --> 00:05:33.601
and I'm going to --
[ Crowd cheers ]

00:05:33.601 --> 00:05:37.033
Is it called Weverse?
-Yeah, Weverse.

00:05:37.033 --> 00:05:39.701
-Weverse, yeah, is
the livestream.

00:05:39.701 --> 00:05:42.067
And sometimes you do karaoke.

00:05:42.067 --> 00:05:44.868
[ Crowd cheers ]

00:05:44.868 --> 00:05:47.334
Sometimes you're cooking.

00:05:47.334 --> 00:05:49.400
This thing that made me laugh,

00:05:49.400 --> 00:05:51.934
this is my favorite
thing you did.

00:05:51.934 --> 00:05:53.067
You fell asleep.

00:05:53.067 --> 00:05:58.501
[ Crowd cheers ]

00:05:58.501 --> 00:06:01.300
You fell asleep.

00:06:01.300 --> 00:06:04.367
And you fell asleep
and just slept for 45 minutes.

00:06:04.367 --> 00:06:09.501
And everyone, 6 million people
tuned in to watch you sleep.

00:06:09.501 --> 00:06:11.400
[ Cheering continues ]

00:06:11.400 --> 00:06:13.334
Did you -- What did you --

00:06:13.334 --> 00:06:16.667
Did you feel sleepy going in?
What happened?

00:06:16.667 --> 00:06:20.200
-I think my fans, ARMY,
liked it because...

00:06:20.200 --> 00:06:23.367
[ Crowd cheers ]

00:06:23.367 --> 00:06:27.968
It was something
very unexpected, but...

00:06:31.267 --> 00:06:34.467
[ Laughter ]

00:06:34.467 --> 00:06:37.734
-Yes, yes.

00:06:37.734 --> 00:06:41.200
I want to do this too.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:41.200 --> 00:06:42.701
I think it's so funny.

00:06:42.701 --> 00:06:45.667
I think it's great.
I'm going to try this.

00:06:45.667 --> 00:06:47.767
Yeah, I know, and we'll see
how many people tune in

00:06:47.767 --> 00:06:50.934
to watch me sleep, but I snore,
so it's going to be rough.

00:06:50.934 --> 00:06:52.601
-I'll see you.
-Okay. You'll watch? Thanks.

00:06:52.601 --> 00:06:55.567
I appreciate it.
Since you've been with the band,

00:06:55.567 --> 00:06:58.033
this is the 10-year
anniversary of BTS.

00:06:58.033 --> 00:07:01.567
[ Crowd cheers ]

00:07:01.567 --> 00:07:04.200
And you guys have been so nice
to come on our show.

00:07:04.200 --> 00:07:06.534
And thank you very much
for always coming on our show.

00:07:06.534 --> 00:07:07.968
We appreciate it.

00:07:07.968 --> 00:07:10.501
I was going to ask you
what's one thing

00:07:10.501 --> 00:07:11.601
that you're most proud of?

00:07:26.400 --> 00:07:27.667
-Yes.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:27.667 --> 00:07:30.834
-That's cool that
you stay humble.

00:07:30.834 --> 00:07:33.367
I want to talk "Golden."
Congrats on this.

00:07:33.367 --> 00:07:36.000
I want to know
about the album title.

00:07:36.000 --> 00:07:40.434
Now, a lot of "Golden" -- Is
that a nickname for you, right?

00:07:42.100 --> 00:07:44.868
[ Crowd cheers ]

00:07:44.868 --> 00:07:48.667
Golden Maknae. What does that
mean, Golden Maknae?

00:07:48.667 --> 00:07:52.534
-It means "golden youngest."
-Okay, yeah.

00:07:52.534 --> 00:07:54.501
-Of the group in Korean.

00:07:54.501 --> 00:07:56.868
-Yeah. And so you --
That stuck with you, Golden?

00:07:56.868 --> 00:07:58.167
And you knew
that was going to be

00:07:58.167 --> 00:08:00.400
the title of the album
always if you went solo?

00:08:06.300 --> 00:08:08.300
[ Crowd cheers ]

00:08:29.534 --> 00:08:30.934
Yeah.

00:08:30.934 --> 00:08:34.467
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:34.467 --> 00:08:37.000
And it's a great cover.

00:08:37.000 --> 00:08:39.133
Great cover. By the way,
look at those abs. Yeah.

00:08:39.133 --> 00:08:47.501
[ Crowd cheers ]

00:08:47.501 --> 00:08:51.067
Never, never. I'll never --
I'll never achieve that, ever.

00:08:51.067 --> 00:08:52.634
I love the album.
It's fun.

00:08:52.634 --> 00:08:56.567
I will say the first half
is very kind of fun.

00:08:56.567 --> 00:08:59.033
It's, you know,
it's Jack Harlow.

00:08:59.033 --> 00:09:03.667
Major Lazer.
It's kind of poppy and fun.

00:09:03.667 --> 00:09:08.234
Second half gets
kind of more serious.

00:09:08.234 --> 00:09:11.133
Some are sad,
sadder than others.

00:09:11.133 --> 00:09:12.100
Is that what you wanted?

00:09:12.100 --> 00:09:13.367
Do you want to be
that versatile?

00:09:42.300 --> 00:09:45.634
Yeah, I think you did it.
I think you did it.

00:09:45.634 --> 00:09:48.634
-Did it!
-Do you --

00:09:48.634 --> 00:09:51.801
Do you run any of the songs
by your bandmates?

00:09:51.801 --> 00:09:53.234
The rest of BTS?

00:09:53.234 --> 00:09:55.367
Because we had Jimin
on the show,

00:09:55.367 --> 00:09:57.901
and he told me that --
[ Crowd cheers ]

00:09:57.901 --> 00:10:00.267
He told me that he runs
his songs by you guys

00:10:00.267 --> 00:10:01.501
before he releases them.

00:10:13.767 --> 00:10:15.267
[ Laughter ]

00:10:15.267 --> 00:10:18.534
Yeah. They're nice.
Yeah. You're family. Yeah.

00:10:18.534 --> 00:10:22.234
Can we say that there may be a
Golden world tour in the future?

00:10:22.234 --> 00:10:26.434
[ Crowd cheers ]

00:10:58.767 --> 00:11:00.934
Yeah.
If you need an opening act,

00:11:00.934 --> 00:11:02.701
I can do two or three songs.

00:11:02.701 --> 00:11:06.801
[ Crowd cheers ]

00:11:06.801 --> 00:11:08.834
-Please.
-Yeah.

00:11:08.834 --> 00:11:10.501
Let's talk about the song
you're performing,

00:11:10.501 --> 00:11:12.801
"Standing Next to You,"
later in the show.

00:11:12.801 --> 00:11:14.133
What does that song mean to you?

00:11:41.000 --> 00:11:47.534
[ Crowd cheers ]

00:11:47.534 --> 00:11:49.367
Is there a little choreography

00:11:49.367 --> 00:11:52.701
from "Standing Next to You" that
you could teach me?

00:11:52.701 --> 00:11:54.400
-Yeah, of course.
-You could teach me?

00:11:54.400 --> 00:11:56.200
-Let's do it. Let's do it.

00:11:56.200 --> 00:11:58.701
[ Crowd cheers ]

00:11:58.701 --> 00:12:01.534
-What do I do?
-Okay.

00:12:01.534 --> 00:12:04.634
So simple.
-Okay.

00:12:04.634 --> 00:12:09.234
-One. Two. Three. Four.

00:12:09.234 --> 00:12:10.467
Oh, yeah.

00:12:10.467 --> 00:12:13.234
Bam, bam.

00:12:13.234 --> 00:12:15.334
♪ Standing next to you ♪

00:12:15.334 --> 00:12:16.200
Bam!

00:12:16.200 --> 00:12:25.300
[ Crowd cheering ]

00:12:25.300 --> 00:12:27.767
-I don't know if --
No, yeah, alright.

00:12:27.767 --> 00:12:30.834
-One, two, three, four.

00:12:30.834 --> 00:12:32.601
Bam, bam.

00:12:32.601 --> 00:12:34.067
♪ Standing next to you ♪

00:12:34.067 --> 00:12:35.167
[ Grunts ]

00:12:35.167 --> 00:12:38.267
[ Crowd cheers ]

00:12:38.267 --> 00:12:40.200
-I can't do that. I can't.

00:12:41.601 --> 00:12:44.467
Can I get a beat maybe?
-You can do it.

00:12:44.467 --> 00:12:46.767
♪♪

00:12:46.767 --> 00:12:49.734
-One, two, three,
four, five, six.

00:12:49.734 --> 00:12:50.868
♪ Standing next to you ♪

00:12:50.868 --> 00:12:52.267
♪ Bah ♪

00:12:52.267 --> 00:12:55.634
[ Crowd cheers ]

00:12:55.634 --> 00:12:56.901
Jungkook, everybody!

00:12:56.901 --> 00:13:00.400
"Golden" is out now.

00:13:00.400 --> 00:13:02.434
And later Jungkook
will be performing

00:13:02.434 --> 00:13:03.834
"Standing Next to You."

00:13:03.834 --> 00:13:04.968
Stick around, everybody!

